    <string name="crash_note">Tap the subject, then use Crash zoom or a volume key. Press again to return. Original framing stays available in the editor.</string>
    <string name="effect_crash_zoom_live_help">A quick push toward a face or detail. Adjust Zoom amount, Speed and Hold, then choose whether to return. During recording, tap the subject and trigger the move with the on-screen control or a volume key.</string>
    <!-- Dolly Zoom. -->
    <string name="effect_dolly_zoom">Dolly Zoom</string>
    <string name="effect_dolly_zoom_summary">Keep the subject steady while the background stretches.</string>
    <string name="effect_dolly_zoom_help">During recording, tap the subject and move slowly toward or away from it; zoom tries to keep the subject the same size. Stop before reaching the lens limit. In the editor, the effect separates subject and background using imported depth or a person mask.</string>
    <string name="effect_dolly_zoom_history">Opposing a camera move with zoom changes perspective while keeping the subject the same size, as in Vertigo (1958).</string>
